<title>USA: U.S. Jan housing starts rose 2.0 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Jan housing starts rose 2.0 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce housing starts and building permits, seasonally adjusted annual rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p> PCT CHANGE: Jan     Dec (Prev)     Nov (Prev)   Jan97/96</p>
<p> -Starts     2.0   -11.0  -12.2     5.6    9.3	 -6.5</p>
<p> -Permits   -1.9     0.3   -0.6     4.1    4.1	  1.2</p>
<p> RATES	 Jan     Dec (Prev)     Nov (Prev)   Jan 1996</p>
<p> -Starts   1,350   1,323  1,329   1,486  1,514	1,444</p>
<p> -Permits  1,395   1,422  1,410   1,418  1,418	1,378</p>
<p> STARTS:     Jan     Dec (Prev)     Nov (Prev)   Jan 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,108   1,005  1,024   1,133  1,161	1,138</p>
<p> -Multiple   242     318    305     353    353	  306</p>
<p> PERMITS     Jan     Dec (Prev)     Nov (Prev)   Jan 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,054   1,015  1,016   1,025  1,025	1,056</p>
<p> -Multiple   341     407    394     393    393	  322</p>
<p> JAN STARTS--Pct--Rate    JAN PERMITS--Pct---Rate--------</p>
<p> -Northeast 22.2   165    -Northeast  -0.7   145</p>
<p> -Midwest  -13.2   256    -Midwest    -6.4   293</p>
<p> -South     -6.8   585    -South	-7.6   593</p>
<p> -West	29.8   344    -West	 13.4   364</p>
<p>Actual Starts and Permits, unadjusted in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	  Jan     Dec (Prev)     Nov (Prev)   Jan 1996</p>
<p>  Starts	81	91     90     112    112	   91</p>
<p>  Permits     88     100     99     102    102	   87</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast January starts at a 1.42 million unit annual rate.</p>
<p>January starts of single-family homes were up 10.2 percent from December, but multiple-unit starts were down 23.9 percent. January permits for single-family units were up 3.8 percent, while permits for multiple unit dwelling were down 16.2 percent.  </p>
<p>The department said the Northeast January starts rate of 165,000 was the highest since 176,000 in November 1994.</p>
